          "reason": "K2_C0001 has a substantively interpretable biological identity: RNA enrichment shows a coherent immune/metabolism phenotype (OXPHOS NES 2.29, interferon responses, DNA repair, mTORC1) and WXS shows a directionally coherent driver pattern (VHL depletion OR 0.128, PBRM1 depletion OR 0.314, BAP1 enrichment OR 30.8). Membership representation is weak and cross-modally mixed (RNA silhouette 0.063 positive; CT -0.035, WSI -0.083, WXS -0.069 negative with high negative fractions), and the pair boundary is only weakly represented (mean silhouettes CT 0.013, WSI 0.050, RNA 0.079, WXS 0.091). However, the pair structural diagnostics show a moderately represented current boundary (within-side affinity 0.6445 vs between-side 0.3969, ARI 0.7442) and the union is single-cluster dominated (candidate_k=1), which is merge-compatible rather than evidence for preserving two units; the normalized-cut cost (0.7733) reflects cross-boundary connectivity but is not positive evidence for distinct units. Internal subdivision is not supported (candidate_k=1, leading eigengap 0.8175 vs 0.1626 at k=2). Measured site/acquisition factors are significantly associated with membership (tissue source site V=0.434 q=0.009; CT phase, scanner model, slice thickness, z-spacing), but these are associations without adjustment and do not specifically limit the biological interpretation; no supported split or merge alternative is available. Given the interpretable, multi-program biological identity and the absence of a supported structural revision, K2_C0001 remains a defensible independent discovery-stage unit."
